  "style": {
    "id": "fireworks",
    "name": "Fireworks",
    "description": "Night-sky fireworks over a harbour whose bursts form planned shapes. A closed-form ballistic shell planner (shells.js) gives each shell a launch time, an apex and a burst; each star flies from the burst centre to its target point of a planned shape (ring, heart, letter, word) under linear drag, then droops under gravity and fades. A per-shell TEMPERATURE loosens the plan: target noise, a random 'take' on the shape (turn, stretch, shear), speed and colour variety, and above a threshold a blend toward plain scatter. Stars, comet tails, flashes and their water reflections are one instanced draw of glowing sprites evaluated in the vertex shader from t. The skyline and water are lit by the bursts (flash colour from the same plan). Sound — lift thump, rising whistle, boom, crackle — is derived from the same shell plan.",
